---
  Agent Role Templates
  Create and inspect role profiles used by spawn_agent.agent_type.
  User templates live in $CODEX_HOME/agents/*.toml.
  Runtime tool catalog: 3 current-thread tools, 1 selected by current policy.

  1. Create new template                   Edit a native TOML role draft for future sub-agent spawns
  2. Create template from current tools    Pick from 3 current-thread runtime tool ids
› 3. [user active] explorer                Role: explorer
                                           Source: user
                                           Status: active
                                           Overrides built-in role with the same name.
                                           Description: Custom explorer role for codebase discovery.
                                           Config file: $CODEX_HOME/agents/
                                           explorer.toml
                                           Config origin: $CODEX_HOME/agents
                                           Native profile fields: name, description,
                                           nickname_candidates, developer_instructions, model,
                                           model_provider, model_reasoning_effort, service_tier
                                           Declaration fields: description, config_file
                                           TOML fields: name, description, developer_instructions,
                                           tool_selection.allowed_tools
                                           Field sources: description=role-file metadata,
                                           config_file=$CODEX_HOME/agents discovery,
                                           developer_instructions=effective role file, name=role-file
                                           metadata, tool_selection.allowed_tools=effective role file
                                           Validation: valid native TOML role file
                                           Runtime use: 3 known threads; 1 running; 1 waiting; 1
                                           closed; current view: yes; thread metadata stores
                                           agent_type, not definition source
                                           Tool selection state: runtime allowlist; unmatched entries
                                           warn during tool planning and grant no access
                                           Runtime catalog reference: current thread planner output;
                                           use as tool id evidence, not as a role-specific preview.
                                           Runtime catalog totals: 3 tools, 1 unmatched current-policy
                                           entries.
                                           Template allowlist vs current catalog: 1 present, 1 absent
                                           Runtime catalog sample: *update_plan (direct), tool_search
                                           (deferred), exec (hidden)
                                           Current unmatched allowlist entries: missing_tool
                                           Template sets: developer_instructions,
                                           tool_selection=update_plan, missing_tool
                                           Runtime binding: spawn_agent.agent_type `explorer`
                                           Enter: open template file for editing
                                           Availability: loaded threads use this TOML file after
                                           native config reload or restart; the TUI wizard triggers
                                           reload after successful create.
                                           Use: ask Codex to spawn a sub-agent with agent_type
                                           `explorer`.
  4. [user tools] Edit tools for explorer  Update this native role TOML allowlist from current tools
  5. [built-in active] default             Default agent.
  6. [built-in shadowed] explorer          Use `explorer` for specific codebase questions.
  7. [built-in active] worker              Use for execution and production work.

  Press enter to confirm or esc to go back
